      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "HfZrTiTa0.53 has a baseline compressive strength of approximately 1314 MPa.",
      "field": "material_initial_state; baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The reported 13.5% terminal strain of HfZrTiTa0.53 is a tensile uniform elongation.",
      "field": "material_initial_state; baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Controlled cold or warm rolling followed by tailored annealing will refine and partially recrystallize HfZrTiTa0.53.",
      "field": "hypothesis; intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10574201::web::019::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The treatment will produce a refined, homogeneous microstructure with reduced grain size and increased grain-boundary density.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10574201::web::019::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Grain refinement strengthens the alloy because grain boundaries impede dislocation motion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10574201::web::019::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Increased grain-boundary density will make plastic deformation more homogeneous in HfZrTiTa0.53.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The refined structure will facilitate enhanced dislocation activity during tensile loading.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10574201::web::019::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Twinning may contribute to tensile deformation after the proposed treatment.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "More homogeneous deformation and enhanced dislocation activity will delay necking and increase uniform elongation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10574201::web::019::5_conclusions",
        "PMC4145285::web::005::tensile_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed treatment will increase tensile uniform elongation from 13.5% to approximately 25–30%.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10574201::web::019::5_conclusions",
        "PMC4145285::web::005::tensile_properties"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed treatment will preserve yield strength near 786 MPa.",
